GCC samples func_2:452; Clang samples func_2:479 (other samples are memcpy).
Those locations are inside the same reached loop at lines 444-520.

Source argument:
The loop is inside if (p_3), so its parameter is nonzero. Its signed i16 union
member starts at 4 and receives a u8 subtraction result after every iteration.
Thereafter it is 0..255 and cannot fail >= -8. The inner u16 loop either breaks
on its nonzero p_3 path or finishes after 0,9,18. Its subsequent g_8=3/<-23
and l_319=0/<-5 loops are skipped, including the only nested return.
The sole outer break tests l_320[2][5] after AND with l_327[8]. These are
initialized to 3 and 0xc538d2c8; their AND is zero and stays zero. No other
executed store in this loop changes that element, mask, or induction member;
there are no function calls. Earlier escaped union addresses do not create
a write in this body. Repeated array initialization explains memcpy samples.

The reduction retains the signed union member, unsigned helper-result
conversion, both inner-loop paths, pointer-based AND and conditional break.
256 diagnostic visits cover one full u8 transition cycle; they are NOT a fuel
limit inserted into the original. UINT32_MAX masks are terminating controls.
This identifies a reached repeating transition, not whole-program definedness
or a terminating checksum. Original seed, source, 10-second limit and label
oracle-unusable remain unchanged. B03 now has 33 identified / 35 undetermined.

